        "text": "Not available at zone level. Of the 218 elements in the synthetic NRC analytics set, only 69 carry any direct containment relation to an IfcSpace in this model — most walls and doors are contained straight in their storey, never in a room. And those 69 elements are attributed to 13 different spaces a combined 130 times over, because the model's RelationText view resolves relations by entity name, and several entities share a name (repeated furniture items, mostly), so the join can't always tell which physical element it's looking at. Rolling that up into a per-zone energy use intensity would be inventing precision the data doesn't have, so I'm not producing one. This is the space-and-zone gap docs/proposals/nrc-deliverables.md's P2 names: no SpaceOfElement view exists yet, and what containment does exist here is too sparse and ambiguous to aggregate.",
